                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Beautiful example of one particular aspect of game design that could ruin the whole game.\n\nFantastic music, brilliant voice, astonishing visuals, handy menu, and terrible, terrible gameplay.\nDisabling controls to teach player is the most frustrating thing ever.\n\nCouple of advices for developer:\n- add \"magnetizing\" of platforms (basically, help player to jump and land more precise);\n- add double- or even triple-jump to avoid replaying the whole level making one small mistake;\n- add \"quick restart\" function without needing to reload the level, just press the key and you're on start;\n- add checkpoints in the level;\n\nMaybe then it would be more playable.\n\nIn current state - no. Just no.",
